      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2013 Asian Oceanian Association for the Study of Obesity . Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "We assessed the metabolic characteristics of high-fat-diet-resistant (DR) rats."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "Body weight, energy intake, locomotor activity, oxygen consumption, plasma leptin and lipid levels, size of visceral-fat adipocytes, and mRNA levels of genes related to lipid metabolism were measured in control rats fed standard chow and in obesity-prone (high-fat-diet-induced obesity, DIO) and DR rats fed a high-fat diet. Glucose tolerance and insulin tolerance tests were also performed."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "DIO rats gained weight more rapidly than did DR and control rats; DR rats gained less weight than did DIO rats despite similar energy intake. Energy expenditure did not differ among the three groups. The diameter of visceral-fat adipocytes was similar in DR and control rats. mRNA levels of genes involved in lipogenesis, such as fatty acid synthase and acetyl-CoA carboxylase, tended to be lower in DR than in control and DIO rats, whereas those of carnitine palmitoyltransferase 1a, which is involved in fatty acid β-oxidation, were greater in DR rats than in the other groups. DIO rats showed hyperinsulinemia and glucose intolerance, whereas DR rats had high sensitivity to insulin."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "DR rats show suppression of lipogenesis and acceleration of fatty acid β-oxidation in the visceral fat. These characteristics likely contribute to the anti-obesity phenotype of DR rats."
          }
        ]
      },
